Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Machine-Gun-Kelly.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

This is a strong draft — the cold open (a good review making him angry), the Type 3 pressure test, and the album-titles table are doing real work. Two things stood out as the biggest problems:

**1. The 2022–2024 window is missing, and it contains the two most on-thesis events of his life.** In December 2023 he blacked out nearly his whole torso and arms in solid black ink — 44 needles, "for spiritual purposes only" — and later rapped "I had a breakdown and tatted my entire body except one line." A man who erases the previous version of himself and leaves one line uncovered *is* the article, rendered on skin, and it's absent. The same track discloses Megan Fox's miscarriage, which is why the Fox section can jump from the 2020 shotgun call straight to "they separated at the end of 2024" and feel like it's skipping something.

**2. The draft never pressure-tests his own confession.** "I got to ruin everything" is quoted as testimony handed over — but he said it on an album-promo podcast, during the cycle, about the cycle. The skeptical read is that "I do it on purpose" is the most flattering story available for addiction, a broken engagement, and a deleted record: it converts wreckage into method. The rabbit hole nods at this; the body doesn't. The good news is the answer is already in the piece — the 2022 therapy quote, said outside any album cycle.

Also flagged: the generational spine is set up ("two nine-year-olds, two generations apart") and never closed on Casie, who per an Aug 2025 People interview talks him *out* of career mistakes; and the piece is dated Aug 2026 but has no anchor newer than Aug 2025, missing the 2026 tour leg and a March 2026 Fox interaction.

Sources: [MGK blackout tattoo](https://www.ladbible.com/entertainment/celebrity/mgk-machine-gun-kelly-blackout-tattoo-body-why-900778-20250922), [Casie Colson Baker](https://www.aol.com/machine-gun-kellys-daughter-casie-214711559.html), [2026 tour](https://au.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/machine-gun-kelly-2026-australia-81260/), [March 2026 Fox comment](https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/mgk-comments-megan-fox-thirst-trap-pics-stoked-had-baby-1236197743/)
